/E (Project Goals)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (The main goal of CleanLink is to create a prototype of a waste cleanup platform that is driven by the community. It will bring together citizen reporting, community fund raising and gig-worker task assignment into one system. On the side the project will show how core data structures such as linked lists, queues, priority queues, hash tables, arrays and sorting, graphs and file handling in C can be used. It will also show how object-oriented design ideas like inheritance, polymorphism, encapsulation and composition in C++ can be applied. Each idea will be used where it fits a need in the system not just as a separate exercise.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (Milestones)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (Milestone 1. Core data and class layer: Build the C data structures like waste spot records, job queues, worker lookup and file storage. Also build the C++ class hierarchy including User, Citizen, Worker, WasteSpot, Job and Campaign. Make inheritance and encapsulation link the two layers correctly.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (Milestone 2. Core workflow: Create the flow from report to verify, fund, assign and complete. Add logic to spot reports and to check before and after photos.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (Milestone 3. Funding, reputation and dashboard: Put in funding thresholds, a clear funding record that only releases money when work is verified a worker CleanScore that shows worker reputation and a simple dashboard that shows spots reported spots cleaned and money raised.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (Milestone 4. Testing and polish: Check edge cases such as reports, campaigns that do not get enough money and disputed verifications. Improve the output and the user interface. Finish the documents and prepare a demo.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
